Description: guard chmod+rm on docs paths that nodoc build doesn't produce
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-17
Bug-Athena: protobuf's override_dh_installdocs-arch in debian/rules
 unconditionally chmods examples/README.md and rm's examples/
 .gitignore from /usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/.  Under
 DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc those files aren't installed by
 dh_installdocs, so the chmod fails with
 "cannot access ... No such file or directory" and the build dies.
 .
 Fix: bracket the chmod with a file-presence test and use `rm -f`
 (silent on missing).  Behaviour without nodoc is identical (the
 file IS present and chmod runs as before).
 .
 TEMPORARY: nodoc is a workaround for missing doc-build tooling in
 the build pool, not a permanent policy.  DELETE THIS PATCH when
 CONF-08 lands and nodoc is dropped from [Source] BuildOptions /
 BuildProfiles in config/build.conf.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -174,8 +174,11 @@ binary-arch: build install
 override_dh_installdocs-arch:
 	dh_installdocs --arch
 	# Fix permission
-	chmod a-x $(CURDIR)/debian/protobuf-compiler/usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/examples/README.md
+	# Athena fork — guard against nodoc build where the docs paths
+	# aren't created by dh_installdocs.
+	[ ! -e $(CURDIR)/debian/protobuf-compiler/usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/examples/README.md ] || \
+		chmod a-x $(CURDIR)/debian/protobuf-compiler/usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/examples/README.md
 	# Remove extra .gitignore
-	rm $(CURDIR)/debian/protobuf-compiler/usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/examples/.gitignore
+	rm -f $(CURDIR)/debian/protobuf-compiler/usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/examples/.gitignore

 override_dh_installdocs-indep:
 	dh_installdocs --indep
